          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: कंकतिका",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कंकतिका — kaṅkatikā — \"a comb\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "kaṅkatikā is kaṅkata \"comb\", already in the Atharvaveda (MW), with the small-thing suffix -ikā. CDIAL 2598 calls kaṅkata of doubtful Indo-European origin, and it lives on as Hindi kaṅghī \"comb\" (CDIAL 2598)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
