              "text": "proñchana \"wiping\" is formed from proñchati \"wipes off\", which MW splits as pra + √uñch. CDIAL 9011 finds that link doubtful and suggests the verb is a Sanskritized Prakrit word, perhaps from Dravidian; Hindi pochnā \"to wipe\" comes from it. Using proñchana for a towel is modern."
